  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts most commonly referred to are the **Terminal Tackle** shirts (for long sleeves) and the **Bahama** shirts (for short sleeves). Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n1. **Terminal Tackle PFG Shirt** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. It features Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, dries quickly, and manages moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n2. **PFG Bahama Shirt** \u2013 Featuring angler-friendly details and lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun so you can stay out there longer. It also has hidden shoulder vents and mesh back lining for extra breathability in hot, muggy conditions.\n\n3. **Tamiami PFG Shirt** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric, UPF 50 sun protection, hidden mesh-lined vents in the back, and an antimicrobial treatment that helps reduce odor.\n\n4. **Tidal Deflector / Terminal Deflector PFG Shirt** \u2013 If you get hot and sweaty on the water, this shirt is great for cooling, made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology that uses touch-activated cooling fabric to prevent overheating.\n\nAll of these are part of the PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, and offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style. The **Terminal Tackle** and **Bahama** are typically the most well-known for being ultra-thin and lightweight.",
